        </div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Boundary Breakpoint Dynamics</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Standard fixed-token chunkers split text mid-sentence or mid-argument, introducing <strong>semantic orphan clauses</strong> that corrupt vector similarity. Semantic chunking dynamically calculates the rolling cosine distance between adjacent sentence embeddings, inserting boundaries only when topic vectors diverge.
        </p>
        <ul class="text-xs text-slate-400 space-y-1.5 font-mono">
          <li>• Reduces context truncation by 41%</li>
          <li>• Eliminates artificial sentence splits</li>
          <li>• Preserves nested JSON & markdown tables</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <a href="/semantic-chunking-vs-fixed-size-rag-benchmarks/" class="text-xs text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 font-semibold inline-flex items-center gap-1">
            Read Semantic Benchmark Study →
